cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Team Peri Peri Fries: a judicial digital evidence
  authentication engine
message: >-
  If you use this software or its methodology, please cite it
  using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Janak
    family-names: Kabra
    affiliation: Vellore Institute of Technology, Vellore
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Jenak26/team-peri-peri-fries'
abstract: >-
  A forensic examination protocol engine for digital video
  exhibits. Rather than emitting a probability of forgery, it
  reports a base-10 likelihood ratio between two explicitly
  stated propositions, declares the validated domain it was
  calibrated on via a Mahalanobis in-domain gate, measures an
  Evidence Fragility Index by adversarially searching for the
  minimum laundering strength at which its own verdict flips,
  abstains with machine-generated reason codes when the
  evidence is too weak or too fragile to report, and seals the
  entire examination in a replayable SHA-256 hash chain that
  reproduces a byte-identical findings hash. Output is
  structured as decision support for a human expert under
  Section 63(4) of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023.
keywords:
  - digital forensics
  - media forensics
  - deepfake detection
  - likelihood ratio
  - ENFSI
  - forensic calibration
  - tamper localization
  - chain of custody
  - reproducibility
